A :PROCEDURE defined inside an SSL data source: its :PARAMETERS is an
ordinary procedure signature, not the data source's interface, so its
defaultless names must not report datasource_default_required (catalog
diag.datasource_default_required: must NOT flag). The script-level
parameter has its inline default. The procedure is called with DoProc.
-- input.ds --
:PARAMETERS sPrefix := "LOT";
:PROCEDURE BuildCode;
:PARAMETERS sHead, nSeq;
:RETURN sHead + "-" + LimsString(nSeq);
:ENDPROC;
:RETURN DoProc("BuildCode", {sPrefix, 1});
-- format --
:PARAMETERS sPrefix := "LOT";
:PROCEDURE BuildCode;
	:PARAMETERS sHead, nSeq;
	:RETURN sHead + "-" + LimsString(nSeq);
:ENDPROC;
:RETURN DoProc("BuildCode", {sPrefix, 1});
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
